{
  "id": "service-discovery-service-discovery",
  "slug": "service-discovery",
  "title": "Service Discovery",
  "category": "Spring Framework",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "what-is-service-discovery",
      "heading": "What is Service Discovery?",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Service Discovery is a design pattern where:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Microservices register themselves with a central registry called the Service Registry.",
            "The registry holds details such as service name, host, port, etc.",
            "Services discover other services by querying the Service Registry to get updated endpoints."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 42,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "benefits-of-service-discovery",
      "heading": "Benefits of Service Discovery",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Services do not rely on static configuration for addresses.",
            "When a service moves to a new host or port, it updates its entry in the registry.",
            "Other services query the registry dynamically to get current details.",
            "This makes the architecture flexible and resilient to change."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "/Users/luffy/Desktop/Computer Science/Infosys/Spring Microservices/Service Discovery/Service%20Discovery/image.png",
          "alt": "image.png",
          "originalPath": "Service%20Discovery/image.png"
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 45,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "components-in-service-discovery-pattern",
      "heading": "Components in Service Discovery Pattern",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Component",
            "Description"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Service Registry",
              "Central server storing details of all registered services."
            ],
            [
              "Service Instance",
              "Each microservice that registers itself with the registry."
            ],
            [
              "Discovery Client",
              "A client inside a service that queries the registry to discover other services."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 37,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "popular-service-registry-solutions",
      "heading": "Popular Service Registry Solutions",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Name",
            "Description"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Netflix Eureka",
              "Popular Java-based service registry by Netflix."
            ],
            [
              "ZooKeeper",
              "Distributed coordination service often used for service discovery."
            ],
            [
              "Consul",
              "Service mesh solution with service discovery and configuration."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 28,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "problem-dynamic-service-instances-in-cloud-environments",
      "heading": "Problem: Dynamic Service Instances in Cloud Environments",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "In CustomerMS, the URI for FriendMS is often statically configured in property files.",
            "In cloud environments, service instances are provisioned and de-provisioned dynamically.",
            "Service instances may run on different hosts and ports at different times.",
            "Hardcoding service URLs is impractical because: "
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 41,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "analogy-changing-phone-numbers",
      "heading": "Analogy: Changing Phone Numbers",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Storing a friend’s phone number statically on your mobile app is like storing static configuration.",
            "If a friend changes their number but you don’t get updated, you get errors when calling.",
            "A global directory app like Truecaller solves this by maintaining a centralized directory of numbers and their owners.",
            "When a number changes, updating the global directory automatically lets users discover the new number."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 64,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "implementing-service-discovery-with-netflix-eureka",
      "heading": "Implementing Service Discovery with Netflix Eureka",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-create-eureka-server-service-registry",
          "heading": "Step 1: Create Eureka Server (Service Registry)",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Create a Spring Boot project named infytel-eureka.",
                "Add dependencies:"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "xml",
              "code": "<dependencyManagement>\n    <dependencies>\n        <dependency>\n            <groupId>org.springframework.cloud</groupId>\n            <artifactId>spring-cloud-dependencies</artifactId>\n            <version>Greenwich.RELEASE</version>\n            <type>pom</type>\n            <scope>import</scope>\n        </dependency>\n    </dependencies>\n</dependencyManagement>\n\n<dependency>\n    <groupId>org.springframework.cloud</groupId>\n    <artifactId>spring-cloud-starter-netflix-eureka-server</artifactId>\n</dependency>",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Configure application.properties:"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "spring.application.name=Eureka1\nserver.port=5555\neureka.client.fetch-registry=false\neureka.client.register-with-eureka=false\neureka.client.service-url.defaultZone=http://localhost:5555/eureka",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Enable Eureka server in the main application class:"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "@EnableEurekaServer\n@SpringBootApplication\npublic class InfytelEurekaApplication { ... }",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 19,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-configure-microservices-as-eureka-clients",
          "heading": "Step 2: Configure Microservices as Eureka Clients",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Add dependency to all microservices (infytel-customer, infytel-friend-family):"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "xml",
              "code": "<dependency>\n    <groupId>org.springframework.cloud</groupId>\n    <artifactId>spring-cloud-starter-netflix-eureka-client</artifactId>\n</dependency>",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Add @EnableDiscoveryClient annotation to the main class of each microservice:"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "@EnableDiscoveryClient\n@SpringBootApplication\npublic class CustomerApplication { ... }",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Add Eureka server URL in microservices application.properties:"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "eureka.client.service-url.defaultZone=http://localhost:5555/eureka",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 24,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "step-3-modify-customerms-to-discover-friendfamilyms-dynamically",
          "heading": "Step 3: Modify CustomerMS to Discover FriendFamilyMS Dynamically",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Autowire the Eureka DiscoveryClient:"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "@Autowired\nprivate DiscoveryClient client;",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Replace static URI with dynamic discovery:"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "List<ServiceInstance> instances = client.getInstances(\"FriendFamilyMS\");\nServiceInstance instance = instances.get(0);\nURI friendUri = instance.getUri();",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Note: The service name in getInstances() matches the microservice's spring.application.name."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 20,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "how-eureka-works",
      "heading": "How Eureka Works",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "@EnableDiscoveryClient: Makes the app a Eureka Client and instance.",
            "Registered instances send heartbeat signals to Eureka server every 30 seconds by default.",
            "If heartbeat is missed, Eureka removes the instance from registry (marks it as down).",
            "Eureka server also acts as a client when clustered.",
            "Clients cache the registry and periodically fetch updates (default 30 seconds)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "/Users/luffy/Desktop/Computer Science/Infosys/Spring Microservices/Service Discovery/Service%20Discovery/1b5b3f02-fbda-4037-a535-e54f1fefb0dc.png",
          "alt": "image.png",
          "originalPath": "Service%20Discovery/1b5b3f02-fbda-4037-a535-e54f1fefb0dc.png"
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 56,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "accessing-service-registry-information",
          "heading": "Accessing Service Registry Information",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Eureka provides a REST API to see registered services:"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "http://{eureka-host}:{eureka-port}/eureka/apps/{spring-application-name}",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 9,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "running-eureka-in-a-cluster",
      "heading": "Running Eureka in a Cluster",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Running multiple Eureka servers prevents single point of failure.",
            "Each Eureka instance registers with its peers and replicates registry info.",
            "Example hosts configuration (in hosts file):"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "",
          "code": "127.0.0.1    Eur1\n127.0.0.1    Eur2\n127.0.0.1    Eur3",
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Sample YAML for three Eureka servers with profiles Eureka1, Eureka2, Eureka3:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "yaml",
          "code": "spring:\n  profiles: Eureka1\n  application:\n    name: Eureka\nserver:\n  port: 2222\neureka:\n  instance:\n    hostname: Eur1\n  client:\n    registerWithEureka: true\n    fetchRegistry: true\n    serviceUrl:\n      defaultZone: http://Eur2:2223/eureka/,http://Eur3:2224/eureka/\n---\nspring:\n  profiles: Eureka2\n  application:\n    name: Eureka\nserver:\n  port: 2223\neureka:\n  instance:\n    hostname: Eur2\n  client:\n    registerWithEureka: true\n    fetchRegistry: true\n    serviceUrl:\n      defaultZone: http://Eur1:2222/eureka/,http://Eur3:2224/eureka/\n---\nspring:\n  profiles: Eureka3\n  application:\n    name: Eureka\nserver:\n  port: 2224\neureka:\n  instance:\n    hostname: Eur3\n  client:\n    registerWithEureka: true\n    fetchRegistry: true\n    serviceUrl:\n      defaultZone: http://Eur1:2222/eureka/,http://Eur2:2223/eureka/",
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Update microservices to point to all Eureka servers in application.properties:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "",
          "code": "eureka.client.service-url.defaultZone=http://Eur1:2222/eureka,http://Eur2:2223/eureka,http://Eur3:2224/eureka",
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 47,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "integrating-ribbon-with-eureka",
      "heading": "Integrating Ribbon with Eureka",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Ribbon can be configured to use Eureka for dynamic service discovery instead of static server lists.",
            "Ribbon fetches the list of active instances from Eureka and load balances only among healthy ones.",
            "This simplifies the client code — no need to maintain static lists."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 44,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "updated-code-using-loadbalanced-resttemplate",
      "heading": "Updated Code Using LoadBalanced RestTemplate",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Autowire RestTemplate with Ribbon load balancing:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "java",
          "code": "@Autowired\n@LoadBalanced\nprivate RestTemplate restTemplate;",
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Call services using service names:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "java",
          "code": "PlanDTO planDTO = \nrestTemplate.getForObject(\"http://PLANMS/plans/\" + custDTO.getCurrentPlan().getPlanId(), PlanDTO.class);\n\nList<Long> friends = \nrestTemplate.getForObject(\"http://FRIENDFAMILYMS/customers/\" + phoneNo + \"/friends\", List.class);",
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Ribbon uses Eureka to resolve PLANMS and FRIENDFAMILYMS service instances."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 21,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "summary",
      "heading": "Summary",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Term",
            "Description"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Service Discovery",
              "Pattern for dynamically locating microservice instances"
            ],
            [
              "Service Registry",
              "Central server storing registered service details (Eureka)"
            ],
            [
              "Discovery Client",
              "Client-side component to query the registry and find services"
            ],
            [
              "Eureka Server",
              "Netflix’s service registry implementation"
            ],
            [
              "Heartbeat",
              "Periodic signal sent by clients to remain registered"
            ],
            [
              "Eureka Cluster",
              "Multiple Eureka servers replicating registry info for fault tolerance"
            ],
            [
              "Ribbon",
              "Client-side load balancer that can integrate with Eureka"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 65,
      "subsections": []
    }
